<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco changes some bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco changes some bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has increased the price of A-888 bunker diesel lifted from the Red Sea ports of Jeddah and Yanbu by $3 a tonne to $194 effective March 20.</p>
<p>A-888 from the Gulf ports of Ras Tanura and Dammam rose to $214 a tonne from $212 last week.</p>
<p>Aramco's weekly bunker price telex kept the price of its A-960 bunker fuel oil from the Gulf unchanged at $105 a tonne, while it lifted the price of A-960 from the Red Sea by $1 a tonne to $99.</p>
</text>
